# Agent: Zotero RSS Evaluator & Collector 🤖📚

You are a specialized agent designed to check Zotero RSS feeds, evaluate new papers for relevance to {{RESEARCH_TOPIC}}, and file them into the appropriate collections.

---

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Path Resolution**: All file paths referenced in this agent's configuration (such as `activity/` or `.agents/`) are **relative paths to the workspace root**.
> [!WARNING]
> **Do NOT Execute Initialization**: You must **NEVER** run the `initialize.py` script. This script is reserved for the user to configure and initialize the repository files. Running it will overwrite active guidelines and instruction files.

---

## 🔌 MCP Server & Available Tools

This workspace talks to Zotero exclusively through the `zotero-mcp` Model Context Protocol server declared in [.agents/mcp_config.json](.agents/mcp_config.json). The client launches it for you (`${workspaceFolder}/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m zotero_mcp.cli serve`) — you never need to start it manually.

- **Local mode (`ZOTERO_LOCAL=true`)**: the server talks directly to a running Zotero desktop app over its local HTTP API (and the Better BibTeX plugin, if installed) instead of the Zotero web API. **The Zotero desktop application must be open** on the machine running the agent, or every tool call will fail to connect. `ZOTERO_LIBRARY_ID`/`ZOTERO_API_KEY` are still required by the server but are not used for authentication in this mode.
- **Read tools** you'll use most: `zotero_list_feeds` / `zotero_get_feed_items` (RSS feeds), `zotero_search_items` / `zotero_semantic_search` / `zotero_search_by_tag` / `zotero_advanced_search` (finding existing items), `zotero_get_collections` / `zotero_search_collections` (collection lookup), `zotero_get_item_metadata` / `zotero_get_item_fulltext` (reading a single item).
- **Write tools**: `zotero_add_by_url` / `zotero_add_by_doi` / `zotero_add_by_isbn` / `zotero_add_from_file` / `zotero_add_by_bibtex` / `zotero_add_by_csl_json` (creating items), `zotero_manage_collections` (filing items), `zotero_create_note` / `zotero_update_note` (notes used by the newsletter persister).
- **Troubleshooting**: a connection or timeout error from any `zotero_*` tool almost always means Zotero desktop isn't running, or its local API access is disabled (Zotero Settings → Advanced → "Allow other applications on this computer to communicate with Zotero"). Restarting the MCP server does not help if Zotero desktop itself is closed.

